From 98a0272e4158b2c20e3a34d210c79b50159af0f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <jufangjian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 03:03:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [rh2-integration] minimal cold recovery: continue the
 published weight version across restart, fail on missing rollout state,
 record run_restarted

RolloutManager.save writes the currently published weight version next to
the data-source state (one integer, same directory and rollout_id) and
RolloutManager.load restores it; the Megatron/FSDP train actors initialise
their updater counter from the restored value (p-1) so the bootstrap
publish is labelled p and the first real update p+1, and the first publish
after a restore is checked against the restored version before the
monotonic/convergence checks. In a recovery context (--load with a
rollout_id >= 0) a missing rollout state file raises RecoveryStateMissing
instead of silently restarting from the head of the dataset. A
run_restarted rh2 event records the restored checkpoint, rollout_id,
published/bootstrap versions and data-source cursor. No joint commit,
COMMITTED marker, replay or composite version identity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
